When running the test specified in tests/test_cat.py in the categorical branch, the test hangs for any valid parameters passed. I have isolated it to the build_model function in test_distributions but have not been able to get further. The likelihood is pretty simple, so I would not expect this to happen.
def categorical_logpdf(value, p):
    if value >= 0 and value <= len(p):
        return log(p[value]).sum()
    else:
        return -inf

def test_categorical():
    for n in [8, 12, 20]:
        yield check_categorical, n

def check_categorical(n):
    pymc_matches_scipy(
        Categorical, Domain(range(2, n, 2), 'int64'), {'p': Simplex(n)},
        lambda value, p: categorical_logpdf(value, p)
        )

In the recent update to allow the multiple traces to be plotted on the same traceplot axes, trace plotting for NpTrace objects was inadvertantly broken. Where the code now reads:
if isinstance(trace, MultiTrace):
    if combined:
        traces = [trace.combined()]
    else:
        traces = trace.traces

it needs to have added:
if isinstance(trace, MultiTrace):
    if combined:
        traces = [trace.combined()]
    else:
        traces = trace.traces
else: #NpTrace
    traces = [trace]

